h for intra-unit/admitted calls so the avoidable per-call cost (the overhead your packet measured between the lowered forms and the direct application) is removed, WITHOUT weakening the guards the adoption and the H3-0 review pinned: admission for anything not statically intra-unit, the outcome-token machinery in tail position, operand evaluation order, and the H3-0 reconciliation's shape-based routing (entry-present callees to admission, entry-absent to invoke-value).\n24\t\n25\t## Required verification (all with real output in your report)\n26\t\n27\t1. The focused gate test: `clojure -M:test -v yang.latte-oracle-test/test-kernel-differential-gate` — after the fix, report the gate's own counts. Expected direction: the two blocked fixtures complete (gate counts drop the :blocked entries); if they pass, the corpus moves to 102 agreements + 2 deviations + 2 upstream failures; the `(:gate-status evidence)` assertion may STILL fail while any admitted arity remains unexercised — state which assertions fail and why.\n28\t2. The Clojure compiler suite: `bb test:sub:clj yang.base` — zero new failures vs master (122+ tests green at last landing).\n29\t3. The exhaustion test you add proves `:consumer v` lands in the ex-data (the carried consumer is the advanced VM).\n30\t4. clj-kondo on every touched file: 0 errors, no new warnings.\n31\t5. Both evaluator lanes agree wherever the harness checks agreement.\n32\t\n33\t## Report\n34\t\n35\tFindings + the exact diff + all command outputs, committed or beside the branch. The kimi quality gate re-reviews before landing."}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_OCN08MrJatd5CwOKrDvVUxz1","content":"1\t# Slice 9 Hardening H3-1 — Blocked Kernel-Gate Fixture Diagnostic Packet\n2\t\n3\t## Status & Governance Notice\n4\t\n5\t- **Slice**: `H3-1` (blocked-fixture diagnosis under the approved Hardening-3 plan)\n6\t- **Branch / Base**: `hardening3-h3-1` based on `0805a25354fb04f90477db6f001bc49e3b84f26c` (`master`)\n7\t- **Production & Gate Source Changes**: **None** (`src/cljc/` untouched; `test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj`, `kernel_gate.edn`, `slice9_evidence.edn`, `slice9_verification.edn`, and `:instruction-budget-per-lane 2000000` untouched). One untracked H3-0 resource file omitted from commit `1fd7236be` (`test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_declarations.edn`) is restored so `yang.latte-oracle-test` loads cleanly in fresh worktrees (see §2.4).\n8\t- **Coverage & Gate Accounting**: Partial and extended-budget traces in this packet are **diagnostic evidence only** and contribute **zero** acceptance or arity coverage credit. The checked-in gate remains honestly `:blocked` (`100` `:pass`, `2` `:recorded-deviation`, `2` `:recorded-upstream-failure`, `2` `:blocked`; `107 / 165` credited arities, `58` `:unexercised`).\n9\t\n10\t---\n11\t\n12\t## Executive Summary & Ranked Root-Cause Hypotheses\n13\t\n14\tNeither blocked fixture suffers from non-termination, unbounded recursion, a shared-runtime (`yin.vm` / `yang.call`) bug, or trace-instrumentation blowup. Both `:check-accepted` and `:check-assume-have-discharge` are deterministic, finite computations whose C lanes execute the exact same UAST and kernel arity sequences and agree with host Clojure (`A`) and the portable source reference (`B`) once given sufficient steps:\n15\t\n16\t- **`:check-accepted`** (`720` traced kernel calls, `2,292` total §8.10 guest calls):\n17\t  - `:c-semantic` **completes at `1,207,270` steps** (within the `2,000,000` budget) and agrees with `A` and `B`.\n18\t  - `:c-walker` reaches **`693 / 720` kernel calls (`96.25%`)** at `2,000,000` steps (already inside the final NbE quotation of `gate-norm-beta-eq?`) and **completes at `2,086,120` steps** (`+86,120` steps / `+4.31%` past `2,000,000`), agreeing with `A`, `B`, and `:c-semantic`.\n19\t- **`:check-assume-have-discharge`** (`2,360` traced kernel calls, `9,598` total §8.10 guest calls):\n20\t  - `:c-semantic` progresses monotonically (`927` calls at `2M` -> `1,924` calls at `4M`) and **completes at `5,030,283` steps** under the `8M` trial, agreeing with `A` and `B`.\n21\t  - `:c-walker` progresses monotonically through the identical call sequence (`459` calls at `2M` -> `1,120` calls at `4M` -> **`2,219 / 2,360` calls [`94.03%`]** at `8M`, already inside the 4th and final `gate-norm-beta-eq?` with only `141` traced calls left). Applying the invariant `1.7280x` walker-to-semantic step multiplier measured across all completing proof fixtures places `:c-walker` completion at **`~8,692,000` steps** (`~692k` steps above the authorized `8M` diagnostic ceiling).\n22\t\n23\t### Root-Cause Hypotheses Ranked by Quantitative Evidence\n24\t\n25\t| Rank | Hypothesis | Share of Measured Cost | Verdict & Mechanism |\n26\t| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n27\t| **H1 (Primary)** | **Clojure §8.10 Common-Call + Outcome Per-Call Lowering Amplification (`src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc`)** | **`95.1% – 95.7%`** of all execution steps (`4,764,636 / 5,009,459` semantic insts on `:check-assume-have-discharge`) | **CONFIRMED PRIMARY CAUSE.** Adopting outcome-wrapped §8.10 common-call descriptors + invoker routing (`ea18c8e47`) raised per-call cost from **`36 -> 538` semantic steps (`14.94x`)** and **`65 -> 934` walker steps (`14.37x`)** for non-tail calls (`37 -> 499` / `69 -> 860` for tail calls). Every call — including intra-unit calls to known `defn`s and `yang/library` sequence helpers — re-mints a fresh admission witness closure and runs structural closure equality (`dsg__admitted?`), builds a 4-key invocation map via nested `conj` closures (`dsg__assoc`), re-validates that compiler-built map (`yang.call/valid-invocation?`), captures a continuation (`u/capture`) on non-tail calls, and unwraps/re-wraps `[:yin.k/ok v]` twice. Actual LaTTe kernel bodies execute in **`32,700` semantic instructions (`0.65%`)**. |\n28\t| **H2 (Secondary)** | **Tree-Walker vs Register-VM Step Granularity (`1.7280x` Invariant Ratio)** | **`+72.8%`** walker steps over semantic steps on identical UAST | **CONFIRMED CAUSE OF `:check-accepted` LANE SPLIT.** `yin.vm.semantic` executes flat register instructions (`1` `:call` instruction evaluates operator + register args; `1` `:branch-false` tests condition). `yin.vm.ast-walker` counts separate CESK steps for `:application` (`:eval-operator`), each `:eval-operand` transition, `:variable` lookups, and `:if` (`:eval-test`). Across all fixtures, `:c-walker` deterministically consumes **`1.7277x – 1.7280x`** steps per `:c-semantic` instruction (`1,207,270 × 1.7280 = 2,086,120`), pushing `:check-accepted` just `+4.31%` over `2,000,000` on `:c-walker` while `:c-semantic` finishes with `792,730` steps to spare. |\n29\t| **H3 (Minor / Observability)** | **Single-Batch Setup Accounting & Missing `:consumer` on Exhaustion (`test/yang/clojure_test.clj`)** | **`1.04% – 1.79%`** of `2M` budget (`20.7k` semantic / `35.9k` walker setup steps) | **CONFIRMED MINOR CONTRIBUTOR + HARNESS DEFECT.** `run-bounded` resets `n = 0` per `(run consumer)` invocation, but `queue-ast!` / `queue-rows!` appends the whole compiled unit in one batch (`:run-calls = 1`), charging setup (`~35.8k` walker / `~20.8k` semantic steps) against the `2M` lane budget. Separately, `run-bounded` throws budget exhaustion without `:consumer v`, causing `observer/consumer-left-by-run` to report the pre-run `loaded` VM (`step 0, :k nil`) instead of the exhausted VM state. |\n30\t| **H4 (Falsified)** | **Infinite Loop / Shared-Runtime Bug / Trace-Stream Overhead** | **`0.28% – 0.38%`** trace overhead (`6` semantic / `11` walker steps per traced call) | **FALSIFIED.** Both fixtures halt with exact `A = B = C` agreement; continuation depth remains bounded (`23 – 48` frames); uninstrumented runs save only `4,330 – 14,170` semantic steps (`7,936` walker steps) and leave every `2M / 4M / 8M` terminal disposition unchanged. |\n31\t\n32\t**Recommended Next Round**: **`compiler fix`** (paired with a 1-line **`harness fix`** in `test/yang/clojure_test.clj:1946` to preserve `:consumer v` on exhaustion, plus tracking `test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_declarations.edn`). Reducing per-call overhead for intra-unit / statically admitted Clojure definitions brings `:check-assume-have-discharge` well under `1,000,000` steps on both lanes without inflating the `2,000,000` gate budget or masking a `14.9x` call-bridge overhead. Full contingent **`budget proposal`** measurements are also provided in §6.2 for architect review.\n33\t\n34\t---\n35\t\n36\t## 1. Pinned Identities, Four-Cell Comparison, and Budget Trial Matrix\n37\t\n38\t### 1.1 Pinned Source, Compiler, and Runtime Identities\n39\t\n40\t| Artifact / Property | Pinned Value |\n41\t| :--- | :--- |\n42\t| **Git Base Commit (`master` / `hardening3-h3-1`)** | `0805a25354fb04f90477db6f001bc49e3b84f26c` |\n43\t| **Upstream `latte-kernel` Revision** | `86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279` |\n44\t| **Gate Adaptation Version** | `{:context 2, :kernel-assembly 4}` |\n45\t| **Configured Gate Budget** | `:instruction-budget-per-lane 2000000` (`test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:1895`) |\n46\t| **Compiler Convention** | `{:outcomes true, :invoker true}` (`arg-vector-opts` + `stream/*` native profiles when instrumented) |\n47\t| **Host Runtime** | Clojure `1.12.4`, Java `17.0.18` (`OpenJDK 64-Bit Server VM`), `Mac OS X` (`aarch64`) |\n48\t| `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc` (SHA-256) | `19328ce01228a800284d7d2cd52d7073f1d7923c7482d46fe9c7df6cb08728a3` |\n49\t| `src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc` (SHA-256) | `51b2f6ecc2b184e7869ddbb8d87dde00d78e6d239258e4e607ddcbdc7bf982d9` |\n50\t| `src/cljc/yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc` (SHA-256) | `7635ea06e2e1f46c96acc5dae31bd2b4bf63b612ec11e65b4c70c5a37ab754d5` |\n51\t| `src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc` (SHA-256) | `32976cf08f911f1189eddcd632ea09bbc9680c8cdcbc129902efe1c0255a7e9e` |\n52\t| `src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/linearize.cljc` (SHA-256) | `ac2a862684a96b30cc5e53daa61b18bf58af0a0561c6ba3b3c019ae37c1e53b7` |\n53\t| `src/cljc/dao/stream/observer.cljc` (SHA-256) | `43020d893eca069fdd10da392474b1c0266a97093bcf8b0135d9d32e0ca14d26` |\n54\t| `test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj` (SHA-256) | `d4655872d46defd3a99de52c11e2fa194ca19b02b1b500e702c106b5cf02bad4` |\n55\t| `test/yang/clojure_test.clj` (SHA-256) | `7443cd4dbdbf574d76297a28bcc2fa2a4de5556d1ed552231971c829eba7405d` |\n56\t| `test/yang/latte_oracle/kernel_gate.edn` (SHA-256) | `f8ea00c01080359e471bbf66fbfbf095dff76c905ec0ecb4ed38c800d15748a4` |\n57\t| `test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_declarations.edn` (SHA-256) | `7fa05e988b4ce6248fefaf68c0dac6d6490b4b279e574b0b93c32b176530d53a` |\n58\t\n59\t### 1.2 Four-Cell Comparison at the Configured 2,000,000 Gate Budget (Instrumented Gate Mode)\n60\t\n61\tBoth fixtures compile `48` `yang/library` definitions plus their static kernel transitive closure (`143` kernel defs / `215,882` AST nodes for `:check-accepted`; `144` kernel defs / `216,917` AST nodes for `:check-assume-have-discharge`). `A` and `B` complete in `< 25 ms` on both fixtures (`[:ok [(λ [A ✳] (λ [x A] x)) (Π [A ✳] (Π [x A] A))]]` for `:check-accepted`; `[:ok [(<a>) (Π [A ✳] (Π [B ✳] (Π [f (Π [⇧ A] B)] (Π [x A] (Π [⇧ A] B)))))]]` for `:check-assume-have-discharge`).\n62\t\n63\t| Cell (`Fixture × Evaluator`) | Mode | Configured Budget | Actual Steps Consumed | Setup / Exec Split | Traced Calls (`Distinct Arities`) | Terminal Reason | Elapsed (`compile / queue+load / run / total` ms) |\n64\t| :--- | :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | :--- | ---: |\n65\t| **`:check-accepted` × `:c-walker`** | Instrumented | `2,000,000` | **`2,000,000`** | `35,707` / `1,964,293` | `693 / 720` (`46`) | `:budget-exhausted` (`Guest instruction budget exhausted`) | `99.3 / 438.8 / 8,625.1 / 9,164.5` |\n66\t| **`:check-accepted` × `:c-semantic`** | Instrumented | `2,000,000` | **`1,207,270`** | `20,715` / `1,186,555` | `720 / 720` (`49`) | **`:completed`** (`halted? true`, `A=B=C` exact match) | `99.3 / 12,415.2 / 2,785.1 / 19,814.3`* |\n67\t| **`:check-assume-have-discharge` × `:c-walker`** | Instrumented | `2,000,000` | **`2,000,000`** | `35,895` / `1,964,105` | `459 / 2,360` (`57`) | `:budget-exhausted` (`Guest instruction budget exhausted`) | `88.2 / 477.8 / 8,636.1 / 9,203.1` |\n68\t| **`:check-assume-have-discharge` × `:c-semantic`** | Instrumented | `2,000,000` | **`2,000,000`** | `20,824` / `1,979,176` | `927 / 2,360` (`87`) | `:budget-exhausted` (`Guest instruction budget exhausted`) | `88.2 / 12,752.7 / 4,638.2 / 24,672.0`* |\n69\t\n70\t*\\*Note on `:c-semantic` `total` ms in diagnostic profiling runs: `total` includes post-run PC-owner table construction (`~4.5–7.1 s`); raw VM execution (`run`) is `2.79 s` (`2.31 µs/step`) vs `:c-walker`'s `8.63 s` (`4.31 µs/step`). `queue+load` on `:c-semantic` (`~12.4 s`) reflects AST-to-datom row projection (`524k–527k` datoms) and linearization (`230,449` / `231,547` instructions).*\n71\t\n72\t### 1.3 Authorized Finite Diagnostic Budget Trials (`2M`, `4M`, `8M`) — Instrumented & Uninstrumented\n73\t\n74\tTrials stopped per cell as soon as completion was observed (`4M` for `:check-accepted` `:c-walker`; `2M` for `:check-accepted` `:c-semantic`; `8M` for both `:check-assume-have-discharge` lanes).\n75\t\n76\t| Fixture | Lane | Mode | Trial Budget | Actual Steps | Setup Steps | Exec Steps | Traced Calls | Progress (`%` of Calls) | Terminal Status | Run Time (`ms`) |\n77\t| :--- | :--- | :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | :--- | ---: |\n78\t| `:check-accepted` | `:c-walker` | Inst | `2,000,000` | `2,000,000` | `35,707` | `1,964,293` | `693` | `96.25%` | `:budget-exhausted` | `8,625.1` |\n79\t| `:check-accepted` | `:c-walker` | Inst | `4,000,000` | **`2,086,120`** | `35,707` | `2,050,413` | **`720`** | **`100.00%`** | **`:completed` (`A=B=C`)** | `9,056.2` |\n80\t| `:check-accepted` | `:c-walker` | Uninst | `2,000,000` | `2,000,000` | `35,691` | `1,964,309` | — | `~96.62%` | `:budget-exhausted` | `8,467.6` |\n81\t| `:check-accepted` | `:c-walker` | Uninst | `4,000,000` | **`2,078,184`** | `35,691` | `2,042,493` | — | **`100.00%`** | **`:completed` (`A=B=C`)** | `8,634.5` |\n82\t| `:check-accepted` | `:c-semantic` | Inst | `2,000,000` | **`1,207,270`** | `20,715` | `1,186,555` | **`720`** | **`100.00%`** | **`:completed` (`A=B=C`)** | `2,785.1` |\n83\t| `:check-accepted` | `:c-semantic` | Uninst | `2,000,000` | **`1,202,940`** | `20,705` | `1,182,235` | — | **`100.00%`** | **`:completed` (`A=B=C`)** | `2,690.1` |\n84\t| `:check-assume-have-discharge` | `:c-walker` | Inst | `2,000,000` | `2,000,000` | `35,895` | `1,964,105` | `459` | `19.45%` | `:budget-exhausted` | `8,636.1` |\n85\t| `:check-assume-have-discharge` | `:c-walker` | Inst | `4,000,000` | `4,000,000` | `35,895` | `3,964,105` | `1,120` | `47.46%` | `:budget-exhausted` | `17,598.7` |\n86\t| `:check-assume-have-discharge` | `:c-walker` | Inst | `8,000,000` | `8,000,000` | `35,895` | `7,964,105` | `2,219` | **`94.03%`** | `:budget-exhausted` | `34,566.8` |\n87\t| `:check-assume-have-discharge` | `:c-walker` | Uninst | `2,000,000` | `2,000,000` | `35,879` | `1,964,121` | — | `~19.5%` | `:budget-exhausted` | `8,691.6` |\n88\t| `:check-assume-have-discharge` | `:c-walker` | Uninst | `4,000,000` | `4,000,000` | `35,879` | `3,964,121` | — | `~47.6%` | `:budget-exhausted` | `17,015.5` |\n89\t| `:check-assume-have-discharge` | `:c-walker` | Uninst | `8,000,000` | `8,000,000` | `35,879` | `7,964,121` | — | **`~94.3%`** | `:budget-exhausted` | `33,754.2` |\n90\t| `:check-assume-have-discharge` | `:c-semantic` | Inst | `2,000,000` | `2,000,000` | `20,824` | `1,979,176` | `927` | `39.28%` | `:budget-exhausted` | `4,638.2` |\n91\t| `:check-assume-have-discharge` | `:c-semantic` | Inst | `4,000,000` | `4,000,000` | `20,824` | `3,979,176` | `1,924` | `81.53%` | `:budget-exhausted` | `9,123.8` |\n92\t| `:check-assume-have-discharge` | `:c-semantic` | Inst | `8,000,000` | **`5,030,283`** | `20,824` | `5,009,459` | **`2,360`** | **`100.00%`** | **`:completed` (`A=B=C`)** | `11,465.0` |\n93\t| `:check-assume-have-discharge` | `:c-semantic` | Uninst | `2,000,000` | `2,000,000` | `20,814` | `1,979,186` | — | `~39.4%` | `:budget-exhausted` | `4,613.2` |\n94\t| `:check-assume-have-discharge` | `:c-semantic` | Uninst | `4,000,000` | `4,000,000` | `20,814` | `3,979,186` | — | `~81.8%` | `:budget-exhausted` | `8,564.7` |\n95\t| `:check-assume-have-discharge` | `:c-semantic` | Uninst | `8,000,000` | **`5,016,113`** | `20,814` | `4,995,299` | — | **`100.00%`** | **`:completed` (`A=B=C`)** | `11,089.9` |\n96\t\n97\t### 1.4 Neighboring Completing Proof Fixtures (Context for the `2,000,000` Cliff)\n98\t\n99\t| Neighbor Fixture | Proof / Theorem Difference vs `:check-accepted` | `:c-walker` Steps | `:c-semantic` Steps | Traced Calls | `Walker / Semantic` Ratio |\n100\t| :--- | :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n101\t| `:elab-accepted` | Same proof `((λ [A :type] (λ [x A] x)))`, calls `elab-proof` only (skips theorem type parse + final `beta-eq?`) | `1,007,668` | `583,252` | `403` | **`1.7277x`** |\n102\t| `:check-rejected` | Same proof, `check-proof` against 1-binder theorem `'(Π [A ✳] A)` instead of 2-binder `'(Π [A ✳] (Π [x A] A))` | `1,728,338` | `1,000,259` | `616` | **`1.7279x`** |\n103\t| **`:check-accepted`** | Same proof, `check-proof` against 2-binder theorem `'(Π [A ✳] (Π [x A] A))` (`+104` kernel calls in second `Π` binder typing & NbE `beta-eq?`) | **`2,086,120`** | **`1,207,270`** | **`720`** | **`1.7280x`** |\n104\t\n105\t`:check-rejected` already consumes `86.4%` of the `2,000,000` walker budget; checking a second `Π` binder in `:check-accepted` adds `104` kernel calls (`+357,782` walker steps) and crosses `2,000,000` by `86,120` steps.\n106\t\n107\t---\n108\t\n109\t## 2. Aggregate Cost, Phase Boundaries, and Observer Step-Counter Audit\n110\t\n111\t### 2.1 Observer Runner Step-Counter Audit (`dao.stream.observer` + `run-bounded`)\n112\t\n113\tWe inspected `src/cljc/dao/stream/observer.cljc` (`run-on-stream`, lines `199–247`) and `test/yang/clojure_test.clj` (`run-guest-machine`, lines `1929–1963`) and ran an empirical multi-batch probe:\n114\t\n115\t1. **Does `run-bounded` reset its step counter across consumer `(run ...)` invocations?**\n116\t   - **Yes in `run-bounded` (`clojure_test.clj:1942–1948`)**: `(loop [v machine, n 0] ...)` binds `n` locally to `0` on each invocation of `run`. In `observer/run-on-stream`, each time `ready?` returns true and `stream/next` yields `{:ok batch}`, `observer` calls `(load consumer batch)` and `(run loaded)`. Our two-batch probe queued two 10-step programs across separate ingress turns under `step-limit 12`: `steps-per-run` recorded `[10 10]` (`total = 20`) and **completed without budget exhaustion** because `n` reset to `0` on the second batch.\n117\t   - **However, in `kernel-c`, `:run-calls` is always `1`**: `tu/queue-ast!` (`walker`) and `tu/queue-rows!` (`semantic`) deposit the entire compiled program (`prelude + yang.call + yang/library + kernel-defs + fixture-call`) as **one** ingress batch (`:load-calls 1`, `:run-calls 1`). Therefore, for every kernel-gate fixture, the reported `2,000,000` count **is** the exact single-invocation whole-fixture total (`setup + execution`).\n118\t2. **Harness Observability Defect on Exhaustion (`clojure_test.clj:1946` vs `observer.cljc:192–196`)**:\n119\t   - `run-bounded` throws `(ex-info \"Guest instruction budget exhausted\" {:lane lane :steps n})` **without** `:consumer v` in `ex-data`.\n120\t   - `observer/consumer-left-by-run` checks `(let [data (ex-data e)] (if (and (map? data) (contains? data :consumer)) (:consumer data) fallback))`, where `fallback` is `loaded` (the VM *before* `(run loaded)` started, at step `0` with `:k nil`!).\n121\t   - Consequently, inspecting `(get-in (ex-data e) [:session :consumer])` on a stock `run-guest-machine` timeout returns the **initial unexecuted VM** (`:k nil`, `:control {:type :application}`) rather than the VM state at step `2,000,000`. Passing `{:lane lane :steps n :consumer v}` fixes this cleanly without affecting gate semantics.\n122\t\n123\t### 2.2 Exact Setup vs Execution Phase Boundaries (Step Numbers)\n124\t\n125\tPhase boundaries were recorded by monitoring VM `:store` population and the `gate-execution-trace` stream at every step:\n126\t\n127\t| Phase Milestone | `:check-accepted` (`:c-walker`) | `:check-accepted` (`:c-semantic`) | `:check-assume-have-discharge` (`:c-walker`) | `:check-assume-have-discharge` (`:c-semantic`) |\n128\t| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n129\t| **1. `dsg__*` + `yang.call/*` prelude loaded** (`yang.call/thrown` in `:store`) | `108` | `66` | `108` | `66` |\n130\t| **2. `yang/library` (`48` defs, `dsg__assoc` + witness minting per def) loaded** | `9,159` | `5,320` | `9,159` | `5,320` |\n131\t| **3. `gate-execution-trace` stream created** | `9,175` | `5,330` | `9,175` | `5,330` |\n132\t| **4. All `143 / 144` kernel `gate-*` descriptors minted & stored (Setup Complete)** | **`35,707`** (`1.79%` of 2M) | **`20,715`** (`1.04%` of 2M) | **`35,895`** (`1.79%` of 2M) | **`20,824`** (`1.04%` of 2M) |\n133\t| **5. `kernel-context` (`env` construction) entered** | `36,536` | `21,196` | `36,724` | `21,305` |\n134\t| **6. Theorem `presyntax/parse-term` entered** (only in `have-discharge`; quoted AST in `accepted`) | — | — | `37,655` | `21,841` |\n135\t| **7. `gate-proof-check-proof` entered** | `37,529` | `21,769` | `388,994` | `224,911` |\n136\t| **8. `gate-proof-compile-proof` entered** | `58,195` | `33,716` | `431,425` | `249,431` |\n137\t| **9. `gate-proof-elab-proof` entered** | `110,725` | `64,079` | `968,309` | `559,035` |\n138\t| **10. `[gate-proof-elab-have 8]` `#1` (`<a>`) entered** | — | — | `1,968,853` (call `#445`) | `1,137,620` (call `#445`) |\n139\t| **11. `[gate-proof-elab-have 8]` `#2` (`<b>`) entered** | — | — | `3,424,782` (call `#913`) | `1,979,658` (call `#913`) |\n140\t| **12. `[gate-proof-elab-discharge 6]` (`×4`: `x`, `f`, `B`, `A`) entered** | — | — | `4,549,964 .. 5,134,105` (`#1295..#1439`) | `2,630,606 .. 2,968,457` (`#1295..#1439`) |\n141\t| **13. `[gate-proof-elab-qed 4]` entered** | `290,654` (`#47`) | `168,116` (`#47`) | `5,455,318` (`#1511`) | `3,154,202` (`#1511`) |\n142\t| **14. Theorem `[gate-typing-rebuild-type 3]` entered** | `1,072,220` (`#415`) | `620,567` (`#415`) | `5,763,120` (`#1590`, 7th call) | `3,332,211` (`#1590`, 7th call) |\n143\t| **15. Final `[gate-norm-beta-eq? 4]` entered** | `1,606,415` (`#608`) | `929,720` (`#608`) | `7,331,479` (`#2096`, 4th call) | `4,239,549` (`#2096`, 4th call) |\n144\t| **16. Halted (`[:yin.k/ok [:ok ...]]`)** | **`2,086,120`** (`#719`) | **`1,207,270`** (`#719`) | *(proj. `~8,692,000`)* | **`5,030,283`** (`#2359`) |\n145\t\n146\t**Key Takeaway**: Loading and descriptor minting for all `191–192` guest functions consumes only **`35,707 – 35,895` walker steps (`1.79%`)** and **`20,715 – 20,824` semantic steps (`1.04%`)**. Over **`98.2%`** of all steps occur during fixture execution after every definition is already in `:store`.\n147\t\n148\t### 2.3 Where Inter-Call Steps Go (`Top Inter-Call Gaps`)\n149\t\n150\tThe largest step gaps between consecutive traced `gate-*` calls occur when kernel functions loop over guest collections via `yang/library` (`map`, `reduce`, `reverse`, `seq`, `rest`, `cons`, `into`, `contains?`):\n151\t\n152\t- `[gate-proof-compile-proof 2] -> [gate-proof-compile-proof 2]` (call `#97 -> #98` in `:check-assume-have-discharge`): **`134,768` walker steps / `77,726` semantic steps** without a single kernel call — spent entirely in `yang/library` sequence manipulation (`seq`, `first`, `rest`, `map`, `reverse`, `into`) compiling the 8-step proof script (`4` `:assume`, `2` `:have`, `1` `:qed` across nested subproofs).\n153\t- `[gate-presyntax-reserved-symbol? 1] -> [gate-proof-check-proof 5]` (call `#68 -> #69`): **`92,079` walker / `53,170` semantic steps** returning unwound outcome tuples up the parsed theorem `(forall [A :type] (forall [B :type] (forall [f (==> A B)] (forall [x A] (==> A B)))))`.\n154\t\n155\t### 2.4 Incidental H3-0 Packaging Finding (`slice9_declarations.edn`)\n156\t\n157\tWhen running `clojure -M:test -n yang.latte-oracle-test -v yang.latte-oracle-test/test-kernel-differential-gate` on a clean worktree from `0805a2535`, namespace load initially failed at `test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:1939` (`(io/resource \"yang/latte_oracle/slice9_declarations.edn\")` returned `nil`). Inspection of commit `1fd7236be` (`c2f8c907..e4d33ce0`) showed that H3-0 staged the 4 modified tracked files (`known-gaps.md`, `slice9_evidence.edn`, `slice9_gate.md`, `latte_oracle_test.clj`) while leaving the newly created `test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_declarations.edn` untracked in the author's worktree. Reconstructing `test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_declarations.edn` verbatim from the load-time contract (`latte_oracle_test.clj:1939–2186`) and `slice9_evidence.edn` passed all `32` assertions in `test-kernel-acceptance-counting` and `test-kernel-gate-evidence-writer-round-trip` (exact replay match against checked-in `slice9_evidence.edn`).\n158\t\n159\t*(Note on CLI invocation: `clojure -M:test -n yang.latte-oracle-test -v yang.latte-oracle-test/test-kernel-differential-gate` requires `-n yang.latte-oracle-test` in fresh worktrees where `build/antlr/*/classes` has not been pre-compiled, per `docs/agents/build-n-test.md:269`.)*\n160\t\n161\t---\n162\t\n163\t## 3. Bounded Snapshots at Budget Exhaustion\n164\t\n165\tAll snapshots were captured via bounded VM accessors (`vm/control`, `vm/continuation`, local `engine/without-store-of` key sets, and the `gate-execution-trace` ringbuffer stream) with zero host-session or closure-environment serialization.\n166\t\n167\t### 3.1 Cell 1: `:check-accepted` × `:c-walker` at `2,000,000` Steps (`96.25%` Complete)\n168\t\n169\t- **State & Progress**: `halted? false`, `blocked? false`, `:store` defs = `205`, traced calls = **`693 / 720`** (`46` distinct arities). Already entered final `[gate-norm-beta-eq? 4]` at step `1,606,415` (call `#608`); only `27` NbE quotation calls (`86,120` walker steps) remain before halting.\n170\t- **Control Position**: `:evaluated-value` (`nil`), local `:env` keys `[k m]` (returning from `dsg__get` inside `yang.call/entry` -> `yang.call/eligible?` -> `yang.call/invoke` while invoking a `yang/library` helper inside `gate-nbe-quotation-`).\n171\t- **Continuation Stack**: Depth **`28`** (`{:eval-operand 24, :eval-operator 1, :eval-test 3}`).\n172\t  - Frames `0..6`: `dsg__get` (`[k m]`) -> `yang.call/_descriptor` -> `yang.call/entry` -> `yang.call/eligible?` (`[callable descriptor ...]`) -> `yang.call/invoke` (`[callable named positional raise ...]`).\n173\t  - Frames `7..9`: `compile-guest-call` escape bridge (`[... coll f res s val dsg__loop0 dsg__raise_escape]`) inside `yang/library` `reduce`/`map` -> `call-entry` (`[dsg__body dsg__invocation ...]`).\n174\t  - Frames `10..11`: `gate-nbe-quotation-` (`[binder f level t tx x x' ...]`).\n175\t- **Top-15 Executed Kernel Call Frequencies at Exhaustion**:\n176\t  `[[gate-syntax-binder? 1] 79]`, `[[gate-syntax-app? 1] 60]`, `[[gate-syntax-kind? 1] 60]`, `[[gate-syntax-variable? 1] 47]`, `[[gate-syntax-type? 1] 40]`, `[[gate-nbe-evaluation 4] 36]`, `[[gate-nbe-quotation- 2] 36]`, `[[gate-syntax-ascription? 1] 30]`, `[[gate-syntax-ref? 1] 30]`, `[[gate-typing-type-of-term 3] 28]`, `[[gate-nbe-evaluation 3] 24]`, `[[gate-nbe-norm 3] 24]`, `[[gate-nbe-quotation 1] 24]`, `[[gate-norm-beta-delta-normalize 3] 24]`, `[[gate-norm-normalize 3] 24]`.\n177\t- **Ordered Tail of Executed-Call Stream (Last 25 of 693)**:\n178\t  ```edn\n179\t  [{:idx 668, :step 1868327, :call [gate-