cljc-287-          :manifest manifest-address\n--\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc-499-   `:segment`: the code space is kernel state.\"\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc-500-  [base entry val]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc-501-  (check-format! base entry)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc-502-  (when-let [defect (effects/continuation-defect entry)]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc-503-    (throw (ex-info \"Corrupt or tampered continuation payload\"\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc-504-                    defect)))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:505:  (when-not (vm/machine-data? val)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc-506-    (throw (ex-info \"Resume value must be plain data\"\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc-507-                    {:rule :resume-value, :val val})))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc-508-  (if (:request-sent entry)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc-509-    (-> base\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc-510-        (update :wait-set (fnil conj [])\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc-511-                (ffi/response-wait-entry entry (:call-id entry)))\n--\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc-714-      (= :branch-false op) [(nth t 1) (inc pc)]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc-715-      (contains? terminators op) []\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc-716-      :else [(inc pc)])))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc-717-\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc-718-\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc-719-(defn- walk-body\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc:720:  \"Breadth-first from `entry` over `successors`, recording every visited\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc-721-   pc's enclosing arity chain (innermost first) into `owner0` and\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc-722-   collecting the `[body-pc chain]` of every nested :closure this walk\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc-723-   passes through -- a :closure instruction's own body is a different\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc-724-   body, scheduled by the caller, never merged into this one; the walk\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc-725-   continues past the :closure instruction itself into the rest of this\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc-726-   body.\n--\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc-280-;; table, successors from the control-flow rule (a tail `:call` has none,\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc-281-;; a non-tail `:call` falls through like any other instruction), then\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc-282-;; `live-in(p) = use(p) + (live-out(p) - def(p))`, `live-out(p) = union\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc-283-;; of live-in(s) over successors s`, iterated to a fixpoint. The fixpoint\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc-284-;; is unique because the transfer functions are monotone over a finite\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc-285-;; lattice (registers ordered by set inclusion), so it does not depend on\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc:286:;; the order pcs are revisited in; pcs are still walked in descending\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc-287-;; order within the body so every host repeats the identical work. Every\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc-288-;; set is a Clojure sorted-set throughout -- its iteration order is\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc-289-;; integer order on every host, so no host map/set iteration order can\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc-290-;; reach the result. `live(call at p) = live-out(p) - {rd}`; this is\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc-291-;; called uniformly for tail and non-tail calls alike, since a tail\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc-292-;; call's empty successor set already makes its live-out, and so its\n--\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc-2494-     pruned, so a guest map shaped like a frame cannot hide a cell ref.\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc-2495-     Only a closure or continuation, a host type no guest can forge,\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc-2496-     re-enters `:kernel` mode through its payload.\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc-2497-\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc-2498-   Scalars hold nothing. With `follow?` a newly found id's content is\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc-2499-   traced too, as data (marking); without, only the refs met directly\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2500:   (pinning). Each value is visited once per mode, so shared environments\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc-2501-   cost one walk and a cell holding its own ref terminates. The worklist\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc-2502-   is explicit: a deep continuation chain does not grow the host stack.\"\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc-2503-  [vm heap roots found follow?]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc-2504-  (let [children-of (if (satisfies? module/IModuleKernel vm)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc-2505-                      #(module/gc-children vm %)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc-2506-                      (constantly nil))]\n--\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/layout.cljc-1157-   continuation in the free environment (§6.3), a retained FFI request\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/layout.cljc-1158-   whose response pair the backend's re-park cannot preserve, and for the register\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/layout.cljc-1159-   kernel a primitive function in the payload data of the run, a wait, a\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/layout.cljc-1160-   ready entry (its state, value, refusal or value-bearing completion\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/layout.cljc-1161-   field) or a parked state (a window, a lexical binding, or reached\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/layout.cljc-1162-   through them), which\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/layout.cljc:1163:   its restore refuses as `:continuation-registers` (`vm/machine-data?`).\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/layout.cljc-1164-   nil when it can.\"\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/layout.cljc-1165-  [task kind]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/layout.cljc-1166-  (let [slots (:slots task)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/layout.cljc-1167-        code (nth slots 11)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/layout.cljc-1168-        collision (image-collision code kind)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/layout.cljc-1169-        free (free-env-procedure task)]"}
