xed** | `disarm!` now sits inside `when-not @(:pending? wake)` on both hosts. `a-nudge-from-inside-a-tick-leaves-the-timer-it-armed-alone` uses a tick that calls `arm!` and then `nudge!`. It requires at least three ticks, and the old ordering would have stranded it at one. A timer can never fire before a queued microtask, so skipping the disarm while the flag is up is safe. | None. |\\n| P3 cadence validation | **Fixed** | `init` refuses a `:factor` that is not a number of at least 1, and a `:ce[...truncated]\ncollab/yin-vm/1792260000000-review-6a-discovery-numbering.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md:94:Applied `collab/1792250000000-docs-amendments-against-master.patch` with `patch -p1` to temporary copies obtained with `git show master:<path>`; it applied cleanly. Both outputs are byte-identical to the landed carrier and continuation documents and the engineer's amended copies.\ncollab/dao-stream/1790536039336-architect-slice5-gate.gpt-6-sol.prompt.md:24:(collab/1790532500000-vm-engineer-node-ws-test-migration.glm-flash.report.md).\ncollab/dao-stream/1792534500000-architect-c3-review.gpt-6-astra.prompt.md:13:Engineer Report: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792532500000-engineer-codec-c3.claude-sonnet-5-5.findings.md\ncollab/yang-python/1792270000000-orchestrator-handoff-python-c4.prompt.md:17:- IN FLIGHT: (a) opus AD-2 in /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ad2 (branch admission-ad2, uncommitted; delete principal-admission and the :admit hook, tests compose :admission, artifact dht-import-v1.edn must stay unchanged; brief collab/1792250000000-engineer-ad2.prompt.md; its report in the worktree's collab/); (b) fable round 2 of the admission-in-linker redesign: collab/1792262000000-architect-admission-in-linker-r2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md (may be finished; if the file is empty or the process is gone and no result exists, re-run the brief collab/1792262000000-architect-admission-in-linker-r2.prompt.md with `claude -p --model claude-fable-5-1 --permission-mode plan`). Round 1 was rejected by codex (collab/1792261000000-reviewer-admission-in-linker.findings.md).\ncollab/yang-python/safepoint-s3/1792390000000-reviewer-safepoint-s3-gate.deepseek-flash.findings.md:11:The reduction adds `(count (filter #{\\newline \\return} text))` per NEWLINE token. The pinned lexer rule (`antlr/python3/Python3Lexer.g4:101`) is `NEWLINE: ({atStartOfInput}? SPACES | ('\\r'? '\\n' | '\\r' | '\\f') SPACES?)`, and `cst/token-record` exports raw `getText`. So a CRLF token `\"\\r\\n\"` advances the line by **2** and a form-feed token `\"\\f\"` by **0**. The design amendment (`yang.antlr.md:1714`) and the function's own docstring both say \"the line breaks\", so `f_lineno` and every line event are wrong for CRLF or form-feed sources. No fixture exercises this (all use LF). Fix: increment once per NEWLINE token whose text contains `\\newline`, `\\return` or `\\formfeed` (the start-of-input SPACES alternative stays 0), and add CRLF + form-feed coverage.\ncollab/yang-python/antlr-multi/1792510000000-engineer-m3-fix.prompt.md:11:READ: collab/1792500000000-reviewer-m3-gate.deepseek-flash.findings.md — the full findings with\ncollab/yang-python/antlr-multi/1792302000000-architect-antlr-multi-reconcile-r2.claude-cloud-fable.findings.md:106:  §2.1 canonical synthetic text in `token-record` (the one JVM exporter edit) and\ncollab/yang-python/antlr-multi/1792302000000-architect-antlr-multi-reconcile-r2.claude-cloud-fable.findings.md:381:`cst.clj` stays, with **one edit**: `token-record` (`cst.clj:157-182`) keeps its\ncollab/yang-python/antlr-multi/1792302000000-architect-antlr-multi-reconcile-r2.claude-cloud-fable.findings.md:752:| M1 IR + exporters + profile | `validate!` rewrite (§1.2) and `conform` (§1.3) with the codex counterexamples, the §1.3.2 acceptance fixtures and mutation table, and the §1.3.3 error checks as tests; `token-record` canonical synthetic text (§2.1, before goldens are generated); `cst/vocabulary`; shared transform; `cst.cljs`, `cst.cljd` with ins